OL,3,GNEWSACentenarian sisters reunited after
OL,4,Afive years apart                       
OL,6,FCentenarian sisters Dot Rawlinson and  
OL,7,FBetty Blood have only been able to keep
OL,8,Fin touch through phone calls and       
OL,9,Fletters over the last five years.      
OL,11,FBut the siblings were finally able to  
OL,12,Fsit down and catch up on a lifetime of 
OL,13,Fmemories thanks to a reunion organised 
OL,14,Fby staff at Haddon Hall Care Home in   
OL,15,FBuxton, Derbyshire.                    
OL,17,FBetty, 101, who lives at the care home,
OL,18,Fspoke of being unable to see Dot, 100, 
OL,19,Fdue to illness and because she lives at
OL,20,FBakewell Cottage Nursing Home, which is
OL,21,Fmore than 10 miles away.               
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
